	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## ADHD\n\nCondition hub: ADHD heterogeneity, competing cognitive accounts, rater-dependent measurement, and the shape of the treatment evidence.\n\n[[ADHD Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-25; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1680,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Constructs and assessment",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1266
		},
		{
			"id": "s0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD - Constructs and assessment|Constructs and assessment index]]**",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD across the lifespan]]**\n*condition* - 5 sources\n\nLifespan presentation, heterogeneity and measurement sources in ADHD, with function distinguished from symptom counts.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD diagnosis and measurement]]**\n*method* - 8 sources\n\nMulti-source assessment, rater and task measurement problems, and the adult-specific limits of retrospective reporting in ADHD.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 762,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Heterogeneity and presentations in ADHD]]**\n*framework* - 6 sources\n\nWhy ADHD is better described as a heterogeneous set of profiles than as one deficit, with consequences for measurement and treatment.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1040,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Rater and measurement effects in ADHD]]**\n*method* - 7 sources\n\nHow parent, teacher, clinician and self-report measures of ADHD diverge, and why that is measurement rather than noise.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1342,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Accounts",
			"x": 420,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 758
		},
		{
			"id": "s1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD - Accounts|Accounts index]]**",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD and prefrontal catecholamines]]**\n*mechanism* - 4 sources\n\nHow prefrontal dopamine and noradrenaline modulate attention, why the relationship is an inverted U, and what the evidence does and does not license.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Reinforcement learning accounts of ADHD]]**\n*theory* - 7 sources\n\nAccounts that explain ADHD-related behaviour through altered reinforcement sensitivity or learning rate, and their evidence.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 786,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Evidence",
			"x": 840,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1012
		},
		{
			"id": "s2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD - Evidence|Evidence index]]**",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[ADHD medication evidence]]**\n*framework* - 4 sources\n\nShort-term randomised evidence, rater and dose effects, tolerability patterns, and the long-term evidence gap in ADHD medication research.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[CBT for adult ADHD]]**\n*framework* - 4 sources\n\nWhat CBT for adult ADHD targets, why comparator and rater determine the result, and how it sits in the wider adult intervention evidence.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 786,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Short-term versus long-term outcomes]]**\n*method* - 7 sources\n\nHow the evidence horizon bounds a treatment claim, what remains open at 26 and 52 weeks, and the certainty tools used to say so.",
			"x": 870,
			"y": 1064,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#FF8FA3"
		},
